  "authored": "2026-09-04",
  "corpus_revision": 4,
  "revision_history": [
    "Revision 4 re-derives the measurement contract against the field map established by the KayakFit convergence and the decompiled official applications. Revision 3 and earlier described five consumed command-6 fields; seventeen are consumed. Fields 1, 7, 10, 12, 14-20 and 23 moved from ignored to consumed, field 23 is consumed leniently and can never reject a frame, and fields 20/21 are unsigned decimal on receive rather than integer. Adds empty, signed, grammar, overflow, bound and leniency cases for every newly consumed index, and a field_semantics block naming the evidence class of all 24 fields. No previously authored expectation was weakened; the corpus had under-claimed what production consumes, so its mutation matrix never exercised twelve indexes.",
    "Revision 3 renames the command-6 field-21 expectation key from power_watts to force_newtons. Field 21 is instantaneous pull force in newtons, never power; the old key encoded the superseded mapping that Phase 1 was supposed to remove everywhere, and it survived in this corpus and in the hardware corpus after production code had been corrected. No value changed - only the label. Found by the section 22.5 phase audit.",
    "Revision 2 distinguishes the zero-field empty line as reject-empty-line while retaining reject-too-few-fields for counts 1 through 23. Revision 1 called all 0 through 23 too-few despite its own stream case and wire specification giving empty lines a distinct rejection. This correction was made during Phase 8.3 before production parser verification; no captured or decoded metric expectation changed."
  ],
  "normative_source": "docs/kayak-first-wire-protocol-spec.md",
  "source_precedence": "Pinned Apache-2.0 TMIW is normative for transmitted behavior under D99. Sanitized QZ debug-ticket traffic is physical-console observation and simulator compatibility evidence, not the command authority.",
  "independence": "Expected outcomes were authored from the Phase 8.1 specification before a production Kayak First parser, framer, writer, transaction coordinator, or simulator exists. Production code must consume this oracle; it must never rewrite or generate it.",
  "transport_contract": {
    "encoding": "UTF-8 with an ASCII protocol subset",
    "delimiter_hex": "0D0A",
    "maximum_outbound_chunk_bytes": 20,
    "maximum_pending_line_bytes": 4096,
    "ack_deadline_ms": 1000,
    "retry_delay_ms": 1000,
    "maximum_attempts": 3,
    "poll_interval_ms": 1000,
    "machine_freshness_ms": 3000
  },
  "measurement_contract": {
    "minimum_field_count": 24,
    "command_field": 0,
    "command_value": "6",
    "consumed_fields": {
      "event_timestamp_ms": 1,
      "active_paddling": 7,
      "distance_m": 9,
      "average_speed_mps": 10,
      "speed_mps": 11,
